@startuml 01-end-to-end-flow
title MOS Aftercare — End-to-End Flow (Activity Diagram)

|Customer|
start
:Reports a fault
(phone call, web form,
or speaks to the voice assistant);

|Intake (Web Form / Voice Assistant)|
if (Channel?) then (Voice)
  :Transcribe the call;
  :Extract fault type, house match,
  error code (stub classifier,
  confidence-scored);
else (Web Form)
  :Search & select the house;
  :Show warranty / commissioning
  status immediately;
endif

if (Safety phrase detected?\n(gas smell / CO alarm)) then (yes)
  #Pink:RULE_01 / RULE_02
  Emergency protocol, P1,
  mandatory human callback.
  Never auto-processed by AI.;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Guided, fault-type-specific
questionnaire — error code / photo
required where the fault type
needs it;

|Triage Engine|
:Look up house record —
installer, commissioning date,
warranty terms, service contract;

if (Commissioning date on file?) then (no)
  #Bisque:RULE_08 — route to
  back-office for manual
  warranty verification;
  note right: priority escalated one level
else (yes)
  if (MOS installed, <=30 days\nsince commissioning?) then (yes)
    :RULE_04 — MOS labour warranty,
    no charge;
  elseif (Installed by a third party?) then (yes)
    :RULE_07 — refer to the
    original installer;
  elseif (Active service contract\ncovers this fault?) then (yes)
    :RULE_06 — covered by
    service contract;
  elseif (In parts warranty AND a\nlikely manufacturer defect?) then (yes)
    :RULE_03 — manufacturer
    warranty claim;
  elseif (Labour warranty\nstill active?) then (yes)
    :RULE_05 — MOS labour warranty,
    no charge;
  else (none apply)
    :RULE_09 — MOS chargeable
    repair;
  endif
endif

:Check for repeat faults at this
site in the last 90 days;
if (2+ prior tickets for the\nsame fault?) then (yes)
  :RULE_10 — flag repeat fault,
  raise priority one level;
else (no)
endif

:Check required evidence for this
fault type (error code / photo);
if (Required evidence missing?) then (yes)
  :Mark ticket dataQuality =
  "incomplete";
else (no)
endif

|Office Admin / Field Technician|
:Ticket created — party, priority,
chargeable flag, and rule
explanation attached;
:Schedule & dispatch according
to priority and assigned party;
:Technician attends, resolves,
and closes the ticket;
stop

@enduml
